<title>FINLAND: Orion at year-high on Fareston go-ahead.</title>
<headline>Orion at year-high on Fareston go-ahead.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Finnish pharmaceutical group Orion B rose sharply on Monday as it said it won U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA) clearance to sell its Fareston breast cancer drug in the United States.</p>
<p>At 1545/1245 gmt, Orion -- already over four percent up ahead of the announcement -- was 10.00 markka or five percent ahead at 210.00 markka, having hit a new year-high 211.00 in lively trade. It last traded at 210.00 markka on May 22.</p>
<p>One broker saw short-term resistance around 215 markka, but said longer-term the stock may have scope to reach 250 markka.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +3589 6805 0247, e-mail news@reuters.fi</p>
